WEBVTT

00:00:14.790 --> 00:00:17.130
Nusumareta kako wo

00:00:17.130 --> 00:00:20.330
Sagashitsuzukete

00:00:21.460 --> 00:00:23.420
Ore wa samayou

00:00:23.420 --> 00:00:27.130
Mishiranu machi wo

00:00:27.330 --> 00:00:32.080
Honou no nioi shimitsuite

00:00:32.330 --> 00:00:33.880
Museru

00:00:34.080 --> 00:00:37.630
Sayonara wa itta hazu da

00:00:37.630 --> 00:00:40.540
Wakareta hazu sa

00:00:40.540 --> 00:00:43.790
Jigoku wo mireba

00:00:44.000 --> 00:00:47.330
Kokoro ga kawaku

00:00:47.460 --> 00:00:52.750
Tatakai wa akita no sa

00:00:54.000 --> 00:00:57.540
Sadame to areba

00:00:57.710 --> 00:01:00.790
Kokoro wo kimeru

00:01:01.040 --> 00:01:05.960
Sottoshite oite kure

00:01:05.960 --> 00:01:07.750
Ashita ni

00:01:07.920 --> 00:01:15.250
Aa tsunagaru kyou gurai

00:01:35.460 --> 00:01:39.040
The armistice which finally ended
the Hundred Years War

00:01:39.040 --> 00:01:41.880
was signed right around the time
I deserted the Melkian army.

00:01:43.000 --> 00:01:44.500
Six months passed.

00:01:45.420 --> 00:01:51.460
My pursuit of the men who had led me
into a trap had led me to the city of Uoodo.

00:02:13.080 --> 00:02:15.420
Triple your money if you hit!

00:02:15.420 --> 00:02:17.170
400 on red-one.
600 on black-five.

00:02:17.250 --> 00:02:22.290
Fyana

00:02:37.540 --> 00:02:40.040
All right, you got him! Now finish him!

00:02:49.460 --> 00:02:50.540
Battling.

00:02:51.170 --> 00:02:56.790
Mock AT combat for gambling by ruffians
who longed for the battlefield.

00:02:58.130 --> 00:03:00.330
But the gamblers were willing to pay even more.

00:03:01.580 --> 00:03:05.250
For the real battles I became involved in.

00:03:06.500 --> 00:03:08.670
Battles with live ammo in our rifles.

00:03:09.210 --> 00:03:11.040
In other words, real combat.

00:03:12.130 --> 00:03:13.960
But that's why the pay-out was so large.

00:03:16.420 --> 00:03:17.750
Two left.

00:03:25.250 --> 00:03:28.290
No fair! This isn't one on one!

00:03:28.290 --> 00:03:30.580
No wonder they offered so much money.

00:03:46.000 --> 00:03:47.000
Draw his fire!

00:03:47.000 --> 00:03:47.920
Roger!

00:04:05.580 --> 00:04:09.330
I see. That's a dirty trick you pulled on him!

00:04:09.790 --> 00:04:12.670
What are you talkin' about?
I didn't want him to go.

00:04:12.670 --> 00:04:14.880
He's the one who okayed all this.

00:04:39.670 --> 00:04:42.920
Despite the winnings,
I wasn't doing it for the money.

00:04:43.670 --> 00:04:48.330
I thought by fighting in these real battles
I might encounter her again.

00:05:56.000 --> 00:05:57.710
We're surrounded!

00:05:58.380 --> 00:06:00.460
Did you sell us out again?

00:06:00.460 --> 00:06:02.880
What kind of girl do you think I am?

00:06:03.380 --> 00:06:04.920
That's why I'm asking!

00:06:04.920 --> 00:06:10.580
It's a trap. That matchmaker must have been
working with the cops to set us up.

00:06:18.250 --> 00:06:20.420
Chirico! Run for it! Run!

00:06:37.420 --> 00:06:38.460
They went in here!

00:06:42.420 --> 00:06:43.290
This way!

00:06:47.790 --> 00:06:49.420
Stop! Stop or I'll shoot!

00:06:49.710 --> 00:06:51.130
If we stop, you will shoot!

00:06:52.290 --> 00:06:53.210
After them!

00:06:54.670 --> 00:06:55.630
Move it!

00:07:06.830 --> 00:07:08.710
There we go. That feels better.

00:07:10.750 --> 00:07:13.670
You must be starving. Take it easy and eat.

00:07:13.670 --> 00:07:16.080
Generous with other people's food, aren't you?

00:07:16.080 --> 00:07:17.250
You got it.

00:07:18.460 --> 00:07:20.630
I'm coming back to life again.

00:07:20.630 --> 00:07:22.920
Thought we'd make ourselves at home.

00:07:23.460 --> 00:07:24.960
By all means, please.

00:07:26.830 --> 00:07:29.670
Now then, Chirico. Can we talk?

00:07:34.130 --> 00:07:36.500
Playing dumb? Knock it off already.

00:07:36.500 --> 00:07:39.920
Why do the cops have it in for you?

00:07:40.880 --> 00:07:42.290
Why do you say that?

00:07:43.830 --> 00:07:45.250
Why?

00:07:45.250 --> 00:07:47.880
They don't usually butt into real battles like that.

00:07:47.880 --> 00:07:51.500
You've got the cops after you
for some other reason.

00:07:51.790 --> 00:07:53.670
I was thinking the same thing.

00:07:55.130 --> 00:07:58.540
That real battle match looked like
a trap for both you and me.

00:07:58.540 --> 00:08:01.960
But the cops were after you specifically.

00:08:01.960 --> 00:08:02.880
Why?

00:08:06.830 --> 00:08:09.830
I'm tired. Will you let me rest?

00:08:11.170 --> 00:08:15.210
It's the war's fault. Nobody's honest anymore.

00:08:15.420 --> 00:08:18.880
If what they had said was true...

00:08:18.880 --> 00:08:21.920
then that mission was the cause of it.

00:09:01.250 --> 00:09:04.540
I assume you've already heard
that Chirico's still alive.

00:09:04.580 --> 00:09:08.170
If worse comes to worst,
we'll be sending you out again.

00:09:08.500 --> 00:09:11.500
In that event, don't show any mercy. Kill him.

00:09:11.920 --> 00:09:15.500
Show us the extent of a Perfect Soldier's power.

00:09:18.540 --> 00:09:19.500
No.

00:09:22.130 --> 00:09:23.170
What did you say?

00:09:24.380 --> 00:09:25.380
I said no!

00:09:32.290 --> 00:09:33.960
Proto One!

00:09:39.830 --> 00:09:42.830
I don't believe it!
A Perfect Soldier, defying orders!

00:09:45.540 --> 00:09:47.710
I knew she was real.

00:09:47.710 --> 00:09:49.500
And that I had to find her.

00:10:00.000 --> 00:10:01.290
Let's go, old man!

00:10:01.580 --> 00:10:04.250
Any time you're ready. The mission disk's all set.

00:10:14.630 --> 00:10:16.670
Turn the rabbit loose, old man!

00:10:16.670 --> 00:10:17.710
Gotcha!

00:10:17.710 --> 00:10:19.000
Here he comes!

00:11:20.420 --> 00:11:23.000
He's behind us! Turn around!

00:11:23.790 --> 00:11:25.130
Back up!

00:11:25.130 --> 00:11:26.630
You go forward!

00:11:52.330 --> 00:11:54.080
It's coming this way!

00:12:01.040 --> 00:12:03.080
Okay, that's ten minutes.

00:12:03.460 --> 00:12:04.380
Let's go.

00:12:04.380 --> 00:12:05.250
Okay.

00:12:51.080 --> 00:12:53.710
But don't forget what we've taught you!

00:12:53.710 --> 00:12:56.080
About what being a Perfect Soldier means!

00:13:35.460 --> 00:13:37.920
Damn it! They got the compressor!

00:13:37.920 --> 00:13:39.210
Chirico, do you read me?

00:13:39.210 --> 00:13:40.460
Where are you? Gotho!

00:13:40.710 --> 00:13:43.710
Behind you, about 50 meters below.

00:13:44.420 --> 00:13:47.880
Watch it. You've still got two or
three choppers hunting you.

00:13:48.420 --> 00:13:51.420
I can't move. Catch me down there
when I get out of here!

00:13:51.420 --> 00:13:52.580
I gotcha.

00:13:53.130 --> 00:13:56.080
C'mon, spread this thing out.
We have to catch Chirico.

00:13:56.080 --> 00:13:56.750
Gotcha!

00:13:56.750 --> 00:13:57.790
Okay, here we go.

00:13:59.130 --> 00:14:00.290
Okay!

00:14:09.630 --> 00:14:13.000
Chirico, can't you fall a little softer?

00:14:13.000 --> 00:14:13.830
Sorry.

00:14:13.830 --> 00:14:17.210
She's all charged up. Let 'em have it!

00:14:18.040 --> 00:14:20.420
Nothing's gonna split us up now.

00:15:00.040 --> 00:15:00.710
Damn!

00:15:11.790 --> 00:15:12.920
There you are.

00:15:30.830 --> 00:15:32.710
Stop the elevator!

00:15:37.630 --> 00:15:39.580
Chirico's broken in! Chirico's broken in!

00:16:40.250 --> 00:16:41.710
We meet again.

00:16:43.000 --> 00:16:44.960
It's always just the two of us, alone.

00:16:50.000 --> 00:16:52.630
We're the only ones in this building now.

00:16:55.670 --> 00:16:58.130
Please, untie me. I won't resist.

00:16:58.580 --> 00:17:01.880
I doubt that rope could stop you
if you wanted to.

00:17:13.580 --> 00:17:15.000
Are you going to kill me?

00:17:21.920 --> 00:17:22.960
What's your name?

00:17:23.670 --> 00:17:24.830
Proto One.

00:17:25.580 --> 00:17:27.330
That isn't a name.

00:17:30.630 --> 00:17:33.250
Proto One is all I've ever been called.

00:17:52.880 --> 00:17:55.960
My consciousness began with my birth.

00:17:55.960 --> 00:17:57.460
With the first thing I saw.

00:17:58.290 --> 00:17:59.830
And that was you.

00:18:01.080 --> 00:18:04.080
It was the first light I saw as I was being born.

00:18:14.080 --> 00:18:15.040
You all right?

00:18:15.040 --> 00:18:17.000
I'm fine! Gotta tell them!

00:18:17.920 --> 00:18:21.380
It's too dangerous to stay here,
now that they know where we are!

00:18:22.750 --> 00:18:26.250
Wait! I came here to see you.

00:18:26.250 --> 00:18:28.460
To ask you what I wanted to know.

00:18:28.460 --> 00:18:30.250
I can't die yet.

00:18:31.460 --> 00:18:32.580
Neither can I.

00:18:39.880 --> 00:18:43.750
Chirico, they can track us
too easily together. Split up!

00:19:08.960 --> 00:19:11.000
Where? Where is he?

00:20:01.500 --> 00:20:02.460
Are you all right?

00:20:02.750 --> 00:20:04.630
Yes, I'm fine.

00:20:14.920 --> 00:20:16.250
Fyana!

00:20:28.380 --> 00:20:29.580
Are you okay?

00:20:30.880 --> 00:20:32.380
Yeah. Thank you.

00:20:57.170 --> 00:20:59.880
Just before, you called me "Fyana."

00:21:03.460 --> 00:21:05.960
Is that a name you've chosen for me?

00:21:07.580 --> 00:21:08.460
It's...

00:21:08.460 --> 00:21:10.880
Well, is it?

00:21:12.670 --> 00:21:14.460
Save that for later.

00:21:14.460 --> 00:21:16.040
We'll have to make a break for it.

00:21:16.040 --> 00:21:17.790
But which way's the escape route?

00:21:18.040 --> 00:21:20.670
Straight that way. We'd better hurry.

00:21:33.880 --> 00:21:35.460
Through that wall.

00:21:39.920 --> 00:21:41.080
Here we go!

00:21:52.040 --> 00:21:53.290
Chirico!

00:21:55.670 --> 00:21:56.830
Fyana...

00:22:01.880 --> 00:22:05.500
Without even thinking about it,
I'd called her Fyana.

00:22:06.420 --> 00:22:07.580
Fyana...

00:22:07.960 --> 00:22:10.710
are you now somewhere in this green hell?

00:22:46.960 --> 00:22:50.710
Fyana, will I ever meet you again?

00:22:53.960 --> 00:22:55.380
Next Episode

00:22:55.710 --> 00:22:58.290
What leads men onto the battlefield?

00:22:58.290 --> 00:23:01.830
For some, they pull the trigger
to earn their daily bread.

00:23:02.000 --> 00:23:05.500
For others, it's to shed their blood for their ideals.

00:23:05.880 --> 00:23:09.080
For others, they surround themselves with
the scent of gunpowder and death

00:23:09.080 --> 00:23:11.250
to achieve their ambitions.

00:23:11.250 --> 00:23:13.380
The rains purify the polluted earth.

00:23:13.380 --> 00:23:16.790
Flowing away to rivers and eventually to the sea.

00:23:17.250 --> 00:23:19.080
Next time, "Upriver"

00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:22.920
Those who resist the flow are overwhelmed.

00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:23.920
Upriver

00:23:19.420 --> 00:23:23.920
Next Time

00:23:42.170 --> 00:23:45.630
Samishii toki mo

00:23:45.630 --> 00:23:49.170
Kanashii toki mo

00:23:49.170 --> 00:23:55.580
Itsumo anata ga me ni ukabu

00:23:56.040 --> 00:23:59.580
Hitori no toki mo

00:23:59.580 --> 00:24:03.000
Aitai toki mo

00:24:03.000 --> 00:24:09.250
Itsumo anata wa mune no naka

00:24:09.250 --> 00:24:12.750
Tooku hanarete itemo

00:24:12.750 --> 00:24:16.170
Tatoe wakarete itemo

00:24:16.380 --> 00:24:22.670
Kono yo no hikari to tomo ni mabushiku

00:24:23.080 --> 00:24:29.000
Ano hi no anata ga...
